/**
\page PlanarPropertiesPage The Planar Figure Properties

The mappers of planar figures, mitk::PlanarFigureVtkMapper2D and
mitk::PlanarFigureVtkMapper3D, read these properties of a data node. Each of
them can also be set for a single render window.

| Property | Type | Default | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| color | ColorProperty | white | Base color. It does not change with the state of the figure; hovering and selection add a halo around it. |
| opacity | FloatProperty | 1 | Opacity of the figure. |
| line width | FloatProperty | 2 | Width of the outline in logical pixels, independent of the zoom. |
| planarfigure.drawname | BoolProperty | false | Shows the name of the node in a label next to the figure. |
| planarfigure.drawquantities | BoolProperty | false | Shows the measurements in the label. |
| font.size | IntProperty | 13 | Font size of the label in points. |
| planarfigure.3drendering | BoolProperty | false | Shows the figure in 3D render windows. |
| planarfigure.3drendering.fill | BoolProperty | false | Fills closed figures in 3D render windows. |
| animated.pulse | BoolProperty | false | Lets the figure grow and shrink by up to 8 percent in 2D render windows. |
| animated.pulse.frequency | FloatProperty | 0.5 | Pulses per second. |

The 2D mapper also reads \c visible, \c selected, which adds a halo, and
\c PlanarFigureInitializedWindow: a figure of locked shape that is being placed
is shown only in the render windows where it is true, i.e. where the
interactor moves it.

Which handles are shown and how they are highlighted does not depend on
properties. mitk::PlanarFigureInteractor reports it to the mapper for the
render window under the mouse.

Scenes of previous versions carry many more properties of the previous
mapper and interactor. Loading such a scene moves \c planarfigure.line.width
to \c line \c width and \c planarfigure.annotations.font.size to \c font.size,
and removes the others.
*/
